(begin-tx "VST-G5 -- the IMMUTABLE claim: a link cannot be created twice")
(env-gasmodel "table")(env-gaslimit 10000000)(env-gas 0)
(namespace "ouronet-ns")
;;==== VST-G5 -- the IMMUTABLE claim: a link cannot be created twice · 01 · env-sigs (caps) ==== ==
(print "--- [VST-G5 -- the IMMUTABLE claim: a link cannot be created twice · 01 · env-sigs (caps)] ---")
(env-sigs [{ "key": "PK_AncientHodler", "caps": [] }])
(print "--- [VST-G5 . 01 . re-creating an existing sleeping link] ---")
;;FOUND BY `python3 tools/_docclaims.py` (IMMUTABLE tier -- added after noticing that "immutable" matched
;;none of the AUTHORITY/BOUND/INVARIANT patterns, and that a permanent property of stored state is
;;the strongest promise a contract makes and the most damaging to get wrong).
;;
;;VST|C_CreateSleepingLink and VST|C_CreateHibernatingLink both say "A ... Link is immutable, and
;;noted in the Token Properties of both DPTFs". VST-04 and VST-06 above create those links on MOCKA
;;and assert they registered -- the POSITIVE half. Nothing asserted the immutable half: that the
;;link cannot then be replaced by creating it again, which is what "immutable" actually promises.
;;
;;THE CLAIM HOLDS, and the mechanism is worth recording because it is not a deliberate guard: the
;;second create dies on the DPOF insert COLLIDING with the existing counterpart row. So a caller
;;gets a raw database error rather than "this DPTF already has a sleeping link". That is the same
;;diagnosability shape as the empty-list index faults in
;;Kursan/_verify_finding_EMPTY-LIST_01_index_iterating_cumulators.repl -- correct behaviour,
;;unhelpful message. Pinned on the stable prefix so it stays meaningful; if a real guard with a
;;readable message is ever added, this fails and the expectation moves to that message.
(map print
    [
        (expect-failure "<<VST-G5>> a sleeping link cannot be re-created -- it is immutable"
            "Value already found while in Insert mode"
            (TS01-C2.VST|C_CreateSleepingLink KST.ANHD (ouronet-ns.DPTF.UR_Konto "MOCKA-98c486052a51") "MOCKA-98c486052a51"))
    ]
)
(commit-tx)

